# {{NAME}}

A decompilation project for **{{TITLE}}** ({{CONSOLE}}, version `{{VERSION}}`; the boot
DOL has sha1 `{{SHA1}}`), bootstrapped by `romwright new-project` (romwright {{ROMWRIGHT}}).
It follows the layout of decomp-toolkit's dtk-template: `config/{{VERSION}}/{config.yml,splits.txt,symbols.txt,build.sha1}`,
`configure.py` writing `build.ninja` and `objdiff.json`, tools fetched into `build/tools/`.

The retail files are not part of this repository and neither is anything derived
from their bytes (`orig/`, `build/` are ignored): the boot DOL is at
`orig/{{VERSION}}/sys/main.dol`{{MODULES_NOTE}}.

## Quick start

```sh
python3 -m pip install -r requirements.txt   # ninja
python3 configure.py                         # fetch tools, `dtk dol split`, write build.ninja + objdiff.json
ninja                                        # link every object, rebuild the DOL, check it against build.sha1
```

A fresh project builds the whole DOL from the assembly-only units dtk writes, and the
last step prints `OK` for each file in `config/{{VERSION}}/build.sha1`.

{{MODULES}} REL module(s) besides the DOL: `ninja rels` links them (`-r`, then `-r1 -lcf`),
runs `dtk rel make` and checks the result against `config/{{VERSION}}/rels.sha1`. dtk's
analysis alone does not reproduce every REL's relocation table (a `.dtors` entry it ties to
the DOL's `__destroy_global_chain` where the retail file points at a function of the module
itself), so that check reports how many RELs are byte-exact and does not gate the DOL.

## What romwright wrote

* `config/{{VERSION}}/symbols.txt`: names, addresses and sizes from romwright's
  analysis, in dtk's grammar. dtk's own analysis runs on top of it and fills in what
  romwright did not name (jump tables, small-data objects); `dtk dol split` writes the
  merged result back, as it does in every dtk project.
* `config/{{VERSION}}/splits.txt`: the `Sections:` block, named and aligned from the
  DOL's own `_rom_copy_info` / `_bss_init_info` tables. Translation units are yours to add
  (`python3 configure.py swap`).
* `config/{{VERSION}}/objects.json`: the translation units that have C: source file,
  whether it is `matching` (linked in place of dtk's object) and per-unit compiler overrides.

