The compiler version is an *era class* chosen from SDK banner dates and the TRK
revision, not a proof of the exact build: a DOL carries no compiler stamp. If a
function will not match at any flag set, try the neighbouring directories of the
compilers bundle (`GC/1.2.5n`, `GC/1.3.2`, `GC/2.6`, `GC/3.0a5`, `Wii/1.3`, `Wii/1.5`):
set `compiler.mw_version` in `config/project.json` (or a unit's `mw_version` in `objects.json`).
Flags are in `compiler.cflags`; they are dtk-template's base set, not calibrated for this game.

## From assembly to C

```sh
python3 configure.py swap fn_80003154            # a function -> its own unit src/fn_80003154.c
ninja                                            # still byte-identical (the unit links dtk's object until it matches)
ninja progress                                   # objdiff report (build/{{VERSION}}/report.json)
romwright-cli match 0x80003154                   # near-miss search over alternative C printings (docs/match.md)
```

A unit whose compiled object equals the retail one is switched on with `"matching": true`
in `objects.json`; from then on the build links your object and the check still has to pass.

## Tools

`config/toolchain.json` pins every tool this project downloads: URL, sha256, version,
license and where the bytes came from. `configure.py` fetches them into `build/tools/` with
`tools/download_tool.py` (standard library only), checking the sha256 before anything is
extracted or run. romwright itself downloads nothing.

* decomp-toolkit {{DTK}} (MIT OR Apache-2.0), wibo (MIT), sjiswrap (MIT OR Apache-2.0)
  and objdiff-cli (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) are open source.
* The Metrowerks CodeWarrior compilers (`{{COMPILER}}` and the rest of the bundle) are
  **proprietary**. They are fetched from the decomp.dev compilers bundle; use them only if
  you are entitled to. Nothing in this repository grants that right.
* To use tools you already have, write a toolchain profile (romwright's `docs/toolchains.md`)
  and pass `python3 configure.py --toolchain profile.json`, or save it as
  `config/toolchain.local.json` (ignored by git). The keys `dtk`, `wibo`, `compiler` (the
  path of `mwcceppc.exe`), `linker` (`mwldeppc.exe`), `sjiswrap` and `objdiff-cli` replace the
  downloaded tool of the same name.
* `--manifest FILE` substitutes another manifest, e.g. one whose URLs are `file://`.
